SUMMARY:[Fairness & Responsible AI][Explainability & Interpretability] ACM 
 FAccT 2027 - Mandatory abstract registration deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: ACM Conference on Fairness\, Accountability\,
  and Transparency\nWebsite: https://facctconference.org/\nSource URL: htt
 ps://facctconference.org/2027/cfp.html\nLocation: Porto\, Portugal\nTopic
 s: Fairness & Responsible AI\, Explainability & Interpretability\, Ethics
  & Governance\, Privacy-preserving ML\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-ba
 sed / interdisciplinary\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-1
 0-28\nNotes: Official 2027 CFP confirms Jun 21-24 and 11:59 PM AoE deadli
 nes\; the author guide makes abstract registration mandatory\, so after O
 ct 27 new papers are closed (OpenReview submission invitation expired by 
 2026-10-28). Homepage and OpenReview venue name Porto\, Portugal (tenth F
 AccT). Camera-ready TBD.\nScope: Fairness\, accountability\, and transpar
 ency in computing\, combining algorithmic research with sociotechnical\, 
 legal\, philosophical\, and human-centered approaches. Characteristic con
 tributions include audits and evaluation practices\, governance\, human e
 xperiences of systems\, and responsible development and deployment. A fai
 rness or accountability question should be substantive\, not a passing mo
 tivation for generic ML.\nAdditional topics: Human-AI Interaction & Deplo
 yment\, Robustness & Safety\nScope sources (2026): https://facctconferenc
 e.org/2026/cfp.html\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://facctconference.org/2027/cfp.html
